1e:["$","$1d","3",{"children":[["$","$1d","0",{"children":[["$","p","0",{"children":["That is why I use the term proof object. A proof object is the specific finished artifact the viewer can judge on screen. It is not the feature category and not the marketing promise. “Study faster” is a claim. “A mnemonic list for four biology terms plus one quiz card” is a proof object. “Organize spending” is a claim. “A sheet with recurring subscriptions grouped by merchant and one flagged duplicate charge” is a proof object. Once the brief names the proof object, the editor can decide three concrete things: what counts as a recognisable result glimpse, which steps are truly necessary, and how long the video must return to the output for inspection."]}]]}]]}]
1f:["$","$1d","4",{"children":[["$","$1d","0",{"children":[["$","p","0",{"children":["A directly relevant archival case is the StudyFetch example, not because it proves performance, but because it is already an app-demo pattern. The archived case section should visibly show readers the post URL, references, and checked date: checked 2026-09-09, based on muted visual inspection, with limitations preserved. What is supportable from that archive is modest and useful: the creator introduces a specific memorisation task, the video shows a filmed laptop with the corresponding prompt, and a mnemonic answer is visible before the clip returns to the creator. That makes it a closer analogue for this article than a food-prep video. It shows problem continuity, visible product action, and a readable output without requiring us to infer unsupported steps or outcomes from a distant category."]}]]}]]}]
2d:T5bc,Below is a completed worked artifact for production use. Proposed data: Search job = “how to memorize biology terms fast.” Proposed data: Audience problem line = “I keep mixing up these four cell-respiration terms.” Proposed data: Proof object = “a review set titled Cell Respiration Review containing four mnemonic lines and one visible quiz card.” Human decision: Result glimpse should show the review-set title plus at least one mnemonic line in a single stable shot. Human decision: Inspectable return should hold long enough for a reviewer to read the title and two complete output lines without pausing. Filled decision rows: Row 1, opening problem: yes, speak or caption the exact study problem in plain language by second 1.5. Row 2, result glimpse: yes, show the completed review set between seconds 1.5 and 3.0; success means the artifact is recognisable as the solved state, not merely a decorative flash of interface chrome. Row 3, minimum steps: show only the note input and the mode selection needed to causally explain the output; omit account setup, idle loading, and unrelated menu tours. Row 4, inspectable return: hold on the generated set for roughly 2 to 3 seconds; success means an internal reviewer can verify title, topic match, and at least two readable lines. Row 5, usage moment: show one quiz card or recall check using the generated material; success means the output is used to complete the job, not just displayed as a claim.20:["$","$1d","5",{"children":[["$","$1d","0",{"children":[["$","p","0",{"children":["$2d"]}]]}]]}]
21:["$","$1d","6",{"children":[["$","$1d","0",{"children":[["$","p","0",{"children":["The execution criteria need to stay concrete because “show the result” is otherwise too loose to review. Result glimpse standard: the shot must answer “what got made?” within about one second, using legible output rather than a generic dashboard view. A glimpse does not need full readability, but it must identify the class of artifact: summary, mnemonic set, itinerary, checklist, or similar. Inspectable return standard: the later hold must let a reviewer confirm that the output materially matches the opening problem. For the study example, that means the terms shown belong to the stated biology task and the mnemonic content is readable enough for a human reviewer to judge whether it is at least plausibly on-topic. APIs do not assess that creative adequacy. That judgment remains editorial and human."]}]]}]]}]
22:["$","$1d","7",{"children":[["$","$1d","0",{"children":[["$","p","0",{"children":["TokPortal is relevant only after the creative is chosen. Its documented delivered-account MP4 preview workflow can validate one exact slot-configuration request against the API’s configuration rules for the current request and current account state, without publishing, replacing the slot, or buying new capacity [2]. That means a team can separately check whether a specific bundle ID, slot position, caption, direct MP4 URL, and future publish date are structurally valid now [2]. It does not tell you whether the result glimpse is clear, whether the inspectable return is long enough, whether the proof object is convincing, or whether later media or platform checks will accept the file for publication [2]. Keep the layers separate: human editors assess creative quality; the dry run assesses request validity under the current contract."]}]]}]]}]
23:["$","$1d","8",{"children":[["$","$1d","0",{"children":[["$","p","0",{"children":["A final boundary matters. TikTok’s For You documentation notes that recommendations depend on multiple factors, and that content not suitable for a broad audience may also be harder to find in search [3]. So even a very clear search-intent structure is not a guarantee of findability, distribution, or downstream product outcomes. The practical value of this framework is narrower: it helps teams build demos that answer a searcher’s job more legibly, document the proof object in the brief, and review the finished cut against explicit human criteria instead of vague taste alone."]}]]}]]}]
24:["$","section",null,{"id":"deep-dive","className":"article-prose deep-dive","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Differentiate the opening question from the proof question"}],[["$","$1d","0",{"children":[["$","p","0",{"children":["Source summary [1]: TikTok says Search helps people explore and learn, and says Creator Search Insights can surface often-searched topics and content-gap topics in select regions. That supports the broad idea that creators should think about query alignment, but it does not prescribe a winning edit order."]}]]}]],["$","figure",null,{"className":"editorial-diagram diagram-compare","children":[["$","figcaption",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mono acid","children":"THE IDEA, UNPACKED"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Two adjacent but different app-demo questions"}]]}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"diagram-items","children":[["$","li","Opening question",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"diagram-index","children":"01"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Opening question"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Problem first or screen first? This is about the first orientation move."}],false]}]]}],["$","li","Current article",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"diagram-index","children":"02"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Current article"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"After a problem-first opening, show steps immediately or show a result glimpse first?"}],false]}]]}],["$","li","Proof object",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"diagram-index","children":"03"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Proof object"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Define the exact finished artifact the viewer can judge."}],false]}]]}],["$","li","Review standard",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"diagram-index","children":"04"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Review standard"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Check recognisable glimpse first, readable inspection later."}],false]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"diagram-caption","children":"Editorial distinction to reduce overlap between related articles."}]]}],[["$","$1d","0",{"children":[["$","$1d","0",{"children":[["$","p","0",{"children":["Source summary [2]: TokPortal’s delivered-account MP4 preview flow checks one requested video-slot configuration on a real delivered account without publishing, replacing the slot, or purchasing capacity. The documentation explicitly limits the preview to current request validation and current account state; it does not prove later media reachability, later platform acceptance, publication, or audience outcome."]}]]}]]}],["$","$1d","1",{"children":[["$","$1d","0",{"children":[["$","p","0",{"children":["Source summary [3]: TikTok says For You recommendations reflect multiple factors and notes that content unsuitable for a broad audience may also be harder to find in search. This is a distribution boundary, not a creative endorsement of any specific demo structure."]}]]}]]}],["$","$1d","2",{"children":[["$","$1d","0",{"children":[["$","p","0",{"children":["The useful editorial distinction is this: article A asks whether to begin with the problem or the screen; article B asks what comes immediately after a problem-first opening. That separation reduces search-intent overlap and gives each page a distinct job. This page is about the proof object and its review criteria, not about the first-frame hook alone."]}]]}]]}],["$","$1d","3",{"children":[["$","$1d","0",{"children":[["$","p","0",{"children":["A good production rule is to separate proposed data from human judgment. Proposed data can include the query target, the proof object, the planned timestamps, and the slot request fields for a later dry run. Human decisions include whether the result glimpse is recognisable, whether the inspectable return is readable, whether the output actually addresses the opening problem, and whether the creative should ship at all. No API in the supplied material assesses those creative questions."]}]]}]]}]]]}]
25:["$","section",null,{"id":"tokportal-workflow","className":"product-workshops","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"case-intro","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mono acid","children":"INSIDE TOKPORTAL"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"From the idea to the actual workflow."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Product screens, documented tools and a practical way to connect them."}]]}],[["$","section","video",{"className":"product-workshop","aria-labelledby":"workshop-video","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"workshop-label mono","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"acid","children":["WORKBENCH / ","VIDEO"]}],["$","span",null,{"children":["DOCUMENTED · ","2026-09-09"]}]]}],["$","h3",null,{"id":"workshop-video","children":"Prepare the actual video slot, not just the caption"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"In the archived editor capture, the interface shows Video, Carousel and Story options, plus a target publishing period. The API example below is a separate documented slot-configuration preview; the screenshot alone does not establish the API contract."}],["$","figure",null,{"className":"product-capture","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/images/tokportal/tokportal-video-editor.png","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","aria-label":"Enlarge: Two real TokPortal editor views showing media format, caption and target publishing period.","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/images/tokportal/tokportal-video-editor.png","alt":"Two real TokPortal editor views showing media format, caption and target publishing period.","width":650,"height":565,"loading":"lazy"}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"children":["Two cropped views of the real video editor, captured 8 September 2026. Historical dates shown; use a valid future window for a new task."," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://app.tokportal.com/dashboard","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","children":"Product ↗"}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"endpoint","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mono","children":"REST EQUIVALENT"}],["$","code",null,{"children":"PUT /api/ext/bundles/{id}/videos/{position}"}]]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"mono muted","children":"ANNOTATED EXAMPLE"}],["$","$L2e",null,{"lang":"en","text":"{\n  \"tool\": \"tokportal_configure_bundle_video\",\n  \"arguments\": {\n    \"id\": \"<real-bundle-uuid>\",\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"body\": {\n      \"video_type\": \"video\",\n      \"video_url\": \"<public_url returned by your video upload>\",\n      \"description\": \"A practical example of organising freelance subscriptions.\",\n      \"target_publish_date\": \"<valid future date: YYYY-MM-DD>\",\n      \"ai_content_disclaimer\": false,\n      \"auto_publish\": false\n    },\n    \"dry_run\": true\n  }\n}","label":"MCP REQUEST"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Replace the marked values with an authorized real bundle, a media URL you control and a valid future date. This is a dry-run template, not an executed campaign. The archived UI shows a two-day period for that captured example; use the current API validation response to determine the dates accepted for your own request."}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"workshop-checks","children":[["$","li","Choose the correct media fields",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mono acid","children":["0",1]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Choose the correct media fields"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"A video needs video_url and description. A TikTok carousel instead needs carousel_images and tiktok_sound_url."}]]}]]}],["$","li","Use a valid window",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mono acid","children":["0",2]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Use a valid window"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Allow at least three days while account creation is pending, or one day for delivered/existing accounts. Check the current response and limits."}]]}]]}],["$","li","Read the preview result",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mono acid","children":["0",3]}],"$L2f"]}]]}],"$L30"]}]]]}]
26:["$","blockquote",null,{"children":["“","After the problem is named, the viewer usually needs proof before procedure.","”"]}]
